 games are non-stabilizing. We conjecture that all parallel chip-firing games\nwith $2|E|-|V|<|\\sigma|<2|E|$ have $T=2$ and thus activity $\\frac{1}{2}$. This\nconjecture has been proven for trees by Bu, Choi, and Xu, cycles by Dall'asta, and\ncomplete graphs by Levine. We extend Levine's method of conjugate configurations to--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSearch Results | Scholarly Articles, Journals, and E-Books | EBSCOhost (https://openurl.ebsco.com/results?bquery=AU+Propp%2C+James&page=1&sid=ebsco%3Aocu.results%3Acrawler)\nciteturn9732search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; ### A greedy chip‐firing game. ...     Journal of Graph Theory, 1995, v. 19, n. 3, p. 411, doi.\n### Who Mourns the Tenth Heegner Number?\n\nPublished in:\n    Math Horizons, 2020, v. 27, n. 2, p. 18, doi. 10.1080/10724117.2019.1648929\nBy:\n    \n\n  * Propp, James\nPublication type:\n    Article\n\n22\n\n### Prof. Engel’s Marvelously Improbable Machines.\n\nPublished in:\n    Math Horizons, 2018, v. 26, n. 2, p. 5, doi. 10.1080/10724117.2018.1518840\nBy:\n    \n\n  * Propp, James\nPublication type:\n    Article\n\n23\n\n### The Paintball Party.\n\nPublished in:\n    Math Horizons, 2017, v. 25, n. 2, p. 18, doi. 10.1080/10724117.2017.11990105\nBy:\n    \n\n  * PROPP, JAMES\nPublication type:\n    Article\n\n24\n\n### Formation of an interface by competitive erosion.\n\nPublished in:\n    Probability Theory & Related Fields, 2017, v. 168, n. 1/2, p. 455, doi. 10.1007/s00440-016-0715-3\nBy:\n    \n\n  * Ganguly, Shirshendu;\n  * Levine, Lionel;\n  * Peres, Yuval;\n  * Propp, James\nPublication type:\n    Article\n\n25\n\n### A greedy chip‐firing game.\n\nPublished in:\n    Random Structures & Algorithms, 2023, v. 62, n. 3, p. 645, doi. 10.1002/rsa.21119\nBy:\n    \n\n  * Li, Rupert;\n  * Propp, James\nPublication type:\n    Article\n\n26\n\n### The fractional chromatic number of mycielski's graphs.\n\nPublished in:\n    Journal of Grap